<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15469" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēlĕvātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		elevo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A lifting up</i>, <i>raising</i>
			(late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manuum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Psa. 140, 2 al.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Gram. t. t., <i>the elevation</i>: vocis (= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρσις</span>, opp. depositio), <i><span class="en">Mart.
				Cap. 9, § 974</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Isid. 1, 16,
			21</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Rhet. t. t., <i>a lessening</i>, <i>disparaging;</i> a species of irony, <i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				2, 50</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 5, §
				525</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
